    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Urothelial carcinoma of the bladder, multifocal, with carcinoma in situ, pT2a pN0 (0 of 18 nodes), margins negative, treated by radical cystoprostatectomy with an ileal conduit; no evidence of disease; under surveillance; synthetic modern detail linked to his documented bladder cancer</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z85.51</td><td>S — Synthetic grade, stage, node count, and margins; the bladder growths, the earlier thiotepa and X-ray therapy, the low-grade malignancy, and the radical cystectomy with a small-intestine conduit are documented (D). Z85.51 is used because the tumor has been removed and no further treatment is directed at it.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Ileal conduit urostomy, right lower abdomen</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z93.6</td><td>S — The small-intestine conduit and the stoma to the right of the navel are documented (D); the coding and the stoma findings are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Acquired absence of the bladder and part of the urethra after radical cystectomy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z90.6</td><td>S — Documented operation (D); synthetic coding.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Acquired absence of the prostate after cystoprostatectomy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z90.79</td><td>S — Documented operation (D); synthetic coding.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Personal history of pelvic radiation for bladder tumor, with earlier intravesical thiotepa</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z92.3</td><td>S — The thiotepa and X-ray therapy are documented (D); the coding and their relevance to the modern episode are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis from the ileal conduit, mild</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E87.22</td><td>S — Synthetic finding at the six-month visit, a known effect of urine contact with the ileal segment.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Acute right pyelonephritis with an ileal conduit (Escherichia coli), with mild acute kidney injury, treated with oral ciprofloxacin and resolved</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>N10</td><td>S — Synthetic intercurrent infection at an unscheduled visit, a common complication of an ileal conduit; it does not echo a documented illness of his after the operation.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

