    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hyperchloremic metabolic acidosis from the ileal conduit (E87.22)</content>. Bicarbonate 20 mmol/L with chloride 110 mmol/L and a normal anion gap, from urine reabsorption across the ileal segment; it can cause tiredness and, over time, bone loss. [S]<list><item>Sodium bicarbonate 650 mg twice daily from today.</item><item>Chemistry again in three months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute pyelonephritis, resolved (N10)</content>. Resolved; creatinine 1.15 mg/dL is back near the baseline of 1.12, and the ultrasound shows no hydronephrosis, so there was no obstruction. [S]<list><item>No further treatment; repeat culture only for symptoms.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bladder cancer after radical cystoprostatectomy, pT2a N0, no evidence of disease (Z85.51)</content>. No symptoms or signs of recurrence six months after surgery. [S]<list><item>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis at one year after surgery.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Chemistry with creatinine, chloride, and bicarbonate</td><td>Every 3 to 6 months in the first year after diversion, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 1.15 mg/dL, eGFR 71; chloride 110 and bicarbonate 20 mmol/L (low): hyperchloremic acidosis; treatment started</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatinine one week after acute kidney injury</td><td>One week after the sick visit</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not done, a deviation from the plan made at the sick visit; he was travelling. Today&apos;s creatinine of 1.15 mg/dL is near the baseline of 1.12, so the kidney injury resolved and no harm resulted. Corrective action: post-illness rechecks are now booked before he leaves the clinic, with a reminder call</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin</td><td>After major surgery until recovered</td><td>Completed today</td><td>13.4 g/dL, recovered from 12.6</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Vitamin B12</td><td>Yearly from two to three years after an ileal diversion</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Baseline normal three months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Upper-tract imaging (renal ultrasound or CT urography)</td><td>Every 6 months to year 3, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Renal ultrasound: no hydronephrosis on either side; normal kidneys</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis (with urographic phase)</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months for 2 to 3 years after cystectomy, then yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At one year after surgery, in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Stoma and peristomal skin</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Skin healed; no leaks since the refit two months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Parastomal and incisional hernia</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine urine culture of conduit urine</td><td>Only for fever, flank pain, or other signs of infection</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Bacteria are expected in conduit urine; no symptoms today</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urethral wash cytology</td><td>Periodically if the urethra is retained and at high risk</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Urethral margin negative and no prostatic urethral involvement</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Fluid intake</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 2 liters a day since the infection</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Leak-free urostomy appliance with healthy peristomal skin. Outcome by 2026-04-07: Appliance refitted with a convex wafer at the consultation; no leaks in the two months after the refit and skin healed [S]</item><item>Stable kidney function (creatinine within 0.3 mg/dL of the post-operative baseline) and bicarbonate 22 mmol/L or more. In progress; target 2026-07-07 [S]</item><item>Regain stamina after surgery: walk 30 minutes a day and regain weight. Outcome by 2026-04-07: Walking 30 minutes most days; weight up 1.1 kg since the first visit [S]</item><item>Written survivorship surveillance schedule in place, shared between urology and primary care. In progress; target 2026-07-07 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Holzbeierlein J, et al. Treatment of Non-Metastatic Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer: AUA/ASCO/SUO Guideline (2017; Amended 2020, 2024). J Urol 2024;212(1):3-10 (2024); Trautner BW, et al. IDSA 2025 Guideline Update on Complicated Urinary Tract Infections (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, urologic cancer monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit in eight weeks. Primary care in three months with chemistry on sodium bicarbonate. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-02: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
